    mission: { situation: ['You are Mika. Your tutor is Daichi. Listen to his new message about what needs checking. Then confirm the facts and the next questions.', 'あなたはミカ役です。講師はダイチ役です。確認すべきことについての新しい伝言を聞き、事実と次の質問を確かめましょう。'], task: ['Explain the change, say what is missing, and ask what approval tells you.', '変更内容と不足している情報を説明し、承認から何が分かるか尋ねましょう。'], roles: ['Daichi', 'Mika'], title: 'Questions for the report check', text: 'Mika, please keep both reports unchanged. We need to ask why the client’s forecast is higher and which research supports it. I have not found that research yet. Kuroda approved the new figures, but we do not know who changed them. Please separate the facts from our questions when we discuss the reports.', lines: ['Mika, what should we do with the two reports?', 'What difference do we need to explain?', 'What supporting information is missing?', 'What do we know about the approval?', 'Does approval tell us who changed the figures?'], evidence: 'Fresh message asks for both reports to remain unchanged, the reason for the higher forecast and supporting research. Research has not been found; it is not proved nonexistent. Approval is known; authorship and intent are unknown. Student may use “higher” without repeating the percentage. Do not introduce exact amounts or accuse Kuroda.', useful: ['The new forecast is higher.', 'We need to ask why ...', 'We have not found ... yet.', 'His approval shows ...', 'It does not prove ...'] },
